--TEST--
A static property read or written through `->` or `?->` is `E0869`, and the message names `P::$x` (`rule:statements/static-is-a-member-modifier`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
final class P {
    public static int $x = 1;
}

P $p = new P();
?P $q = $p;
echo $p->x, "\n";
echo $q?->x, "\n";
$p->x = 3;
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0869]: `P::$x` is static, so an object does not have it
%A
8 | echo $p->x, "\n";
%A
  = help: write `P::$x`
%A
error[E0869]: `P::$x` is static, so an object does not have it
%A
9 | echo $q?->x, "\n";
%A
error[E0869]: `P::$x` is static, so an object does not have it
%A
10 | $p->x = 3;
%A
error: aborting due to 3 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
